  "limits": [
    "This is a reusable one-purchase scheduler, not the released multi-hop transport/admission driver or automatic replenishment",
    "The application retains the original random job ID for resume; automatic encrypted-job discovery is not provided",
    "Requires initialized encrypted payer/index books, existing authenticated owned notes, separately accepted pins/prover and a funded dedicated native relayer",
    "Exact native recovery scans at most 65536 attempts in the local relayer journal; high-volume scheduling optimization remains open",
    "Purchase request windows are finite; ambiguous requests retain their exact identities and expiry, with no implicit renewal or extra spending consent",
    "Retain original funding/native witnesses before pruning and extend them to accepted checkpoints; general long-history and backup/key-custody tooling remain open",
    "No funded private per-hop kernel route, combined route restart/ExEx, production proving-key ceremony or independent cryptographic review was performed here",
    "Native deposits/withdrawals, relayer identity and timing remain public; tunnel encryption does not hide all metadata or protect plaintext beyond the exit"
  ],
